      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The diagnosis of the cause of upper abdominal pain has been considerably aided in recent times by the increasing availability of endoscopic and imaging techniques. Patient management may be sub-optimal, however, if this technology is used inappropriately, particularly if the continued importance of taking a full history is overlooked, and the hazards arising from the pursuit of incidental findings are not appreciated."},
